"""
## Purpose and audience
Purpose: Pin the vector parts Chrome paints inside the media controls of an
`<audio controls>` and a `<video controls>` that have no media: the play
triangle, the timeline track, the volume icon and the overflow (kebab) dots of
the audio strip, and the timeline track and kebab dots of a narrow video.
Before this spec the renderer painted only the audio pill and the video scrim,
which left 1,015 (audio) and 388 (video) mismatching pixels at 1x on the web
catalog's `animation` page (11,629 and 6,059 at device scale 4).
Audience: browser-engine paint maintainers.

Chrome oracle: Chrome for Testing 159 headless, `--window-size=400,300`, device
scale 1 and 4, pixels read from the PNG. Page (PAGE below): a 300x54 audio at
(10,10), a 120x150 video at (10,74), a 230x60 video at (10,234).

Measured geometry (CSS px, relative to the control's content box, w x h):

| part                | geometry                                                       | paint            |
|---------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|------------------|
| audio play          | Material `play_arrow` (8,5) (8,19) (19,12) at 20/24, icon box 20x20 at (16, h/2-10) | black at 30 % |
| audio timeline      | 4 px stadium, x 129.27 (1x: 129.08) .. w-90, centred on h/2   | black at 20 %    |
| audio volume        | Material `volume_up` at 20/24, icon box at (w-68, h/2-10)       | black at 30 %    |
| audio kebab         | three r=2 dots (x 20/24), 6 units apart, icon box at (w-36, h/2-10) | black         |
| video timeline      | 4 px stadium, x 16 .. w-16, y h-24 .. h-20                      | white at 30 %    |
| video kebab         | the same dots, centred on (w-24, h-48)                          | white at 30 %    |

The audio timeline's left end follows the `0:00 / 0:00` time text (AC-8:
14px Liberation Sans #1f1f1f, measured 2026-11-24: `0:00` at x 47 and `/ 0:00`
at x 78.25 of the content box, two boxes, on a `normal` line centred in the
strip; Chrome paints it LCD at 1x, gray at 4x); 129.27 (129.08 at device
scale 1, where the text advances differ) is the track position with that face.
Base 0ba06362020 paints no time text (4x: 2825 Chrome ink px missing).

The 1x references are Chrome's pixels; a pixel counts as a mismatch when any
channel is off by more than 8. At device scale 4 the ink box and ink count of
each part are compared (box within 1 device px, count within 4 %).
"""

"""
Traceability: REQ-BROWSER-ENGINE-REPLACED-005 — the media-controls vector parts of audio and video paint as Chrome 159 paints them, at device scale 1 and 4
"""
# @tag: unit, browser_engine, paint, media_controls, device_scale, chrome159
# @cover src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/media_control_chrome.spl 1%
